# Arabic (Saudi) translation for ai_operations_chat_widget.
#
# The widget is the product's own surface and every string in it is English. In
# an Arabic-first demo that reads as a half-translated product, and it is the
# panel a customer looks at for the whole presentation.
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE DOES NOT TAKE EFFECT YET. The terms live in a static QWeb asset
# (static/src/chat_widget.xml), and on this build they are not picked up by the
# module's translation import: the panel still renders English after a module
# update and a server restart, with the reference lines in both the
# model_terms and the code:addons form. The kernel's own ar_001.po works, so the
# mechanism is right for Python terms and something about static asset
# extraction is not. The Arabic below is correct and reviewed; what is missing
# is whatever makes Odoo serve it. Recorded as a known limitation rather than
# deleted, because the translation is not the part that is wrong.
msgid ""
msgstr ""
